WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.720
Who would have thought that the cheerfully vulgar&nbsp;
stunt show "Jackass" would prove to be one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:09.760
most enduring media properties of the 21st&nbsp;
century? Whether or not you placed money on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:16.400
its success, the fourth feature-length film of the&nbsp;
franchise is set to debut on October 22nd, 2021.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:21.040
In fact, a brand-new trailer for "Jackass Forever"&nbsp;
just dropped and if you're a long-time fan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.360
you might have noticed a disappointing absence.

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:28.320
The trailer for "Jackass Forever" begins with a&nbsp;
peppy song and title cards asking the question,

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.920
"When was the last time you got together&nbsp;
with old friends to laugh your asses off?"

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.080
What follows is two minutes of pure&nbsp;
tomfoolery as Johnny Knoxville, Steve-O,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:40.480
and "Jackass" team members old and new&nbsp;
participate in a series of death-defying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:45.200
stunts that will have you wincing in discomfort&nbsp;
and howling with laughter in equal measure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:49.360
It's clear, though, that one old friend&nbsp;
is missing from the chaos: Bam Margera.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:53.440
Not only is Margera absent from the&nbsp;
teases for "Jackass Forever" itself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.760
but he's also not prominently featured in&nbsp;
any of the archival footage that appears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:02.400
in the trailer. If you grew up watching him on&nbsp;
"Jackass" or his spin-off series "Viva La Bam,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.800
you're likely curious about his absence.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:11.040
Back in February 2021, Margera posted a series of&nbsp;
videos to his personal Instagram page claiming,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:15.200
among other things, that he had been booted&nbsp;
from the production of "Jackass Forever”.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.800
Margera said in the video,

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:21.280
"'Jackass' does not care about me. Understand&nbsp;
that, ladies and gentlemen ... It was like my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:25.360
family, it won't let me in because they&nbsp;
say I'm out there being a jackass on TMZ.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:28.640
So I can't be in 'Jackass' because&nbsp;
I'm out there being a jackass?"

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:32.880
In April, TMZ followed up with Margera&nbsp;
about this relationship with the film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:36.800
During a taped interview, he claimed that&nbsp;
he was pressured by somebody in production&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:41.520
to do a 90-day stint in rehab, which resulted&nbsp;
in him being placed on a number of different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:47.280
medications. Margera says this led to him&nbsp;
experiencing "suicidal tendencies," telling TMZ,

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:50.720
"What's the point of a five million&nbsp;
dollar contract that I have to walk on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:55.200
eggshells and jump through your hoops — which&nbsp;
is already impossible — to obey if I'm dead?"

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.280
He called the experience "torture" and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:00.800
implied that he planned on taking&nbsp;
legal action against production.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:04.720
"It's supposed to be a f—ing reunion&nbsp;
... to pay our respects to Ryan Dunn."

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:08.480
Dunn, one of the original stars&nbsp;
of the franchise, died in 2011.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:10.720
During his criticism of the film's production,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:14.800
Margera called out several members of&nbsp;
the crew specifically, including Johnny&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:19.520
Knoxville. Director Jeff Tremaine ended up&nbsp;
filing a restraining order against Margera.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:25.760
During a May 2021 profile in GQ, Johnny Knoxville&nbsp;
took the time to touch on Margera's accusations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:30.560
and ultimate absence from "Jackass Forever."&nbsp;
Although he didn't delve deep into the details&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:34.480
of the situation, it's clear that the&nbsp;
episode was painful for Knoxville.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:38.480
"We want Bam to be happy and healthy and&nbsp;
get the help he needs. We tried to push&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:41.760
that along. I think that's all I really&nbsp;
want to say about it ... I don't want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:45.440
to get into public back-and-forth with&nbsp;
Bam ... I just want him to get better."

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:49.520
Speaking generally about mental health and&nbsp;
substance abuse issues that various cast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:52.160
members have faced over the years, Knoxville said,

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:55.760
"I think each of us was responsible for&nbsp;
his own actions ... And when someone's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:58.080
struggling, everyone tries to help that person.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:02.560
And at the end of the day, that person has&nbsp;
to want help. Sometimes they don't. Yet."

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:07.680
"Jackass Forever" is slated to hit&nbsp;
theaters on October 22nd, 2021.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:12.320
If you or anyone you know is struggling with&nbsp;
addiction issues, help is available. Visit the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:14.880
Substance Abuse and Mental Health Services&nbsp;
Administration website or contact SAMHSA's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:25.120
National Helpline at 1-800-662-HELP (4357).

